      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is an interesting issue and i\u0027m not sure there is \"correct\" answer. But, I feel like we, optionally, only want to capture what is used. In other words, if I load 100 textures and have 100 buffers but during the capture I only reference 2 of each, then I think I\u0027d prefer it only capture those 4 objects?\n\nIf that\u0027s good, then I\u0027d expect the design to be more of the pattern of for each resource used, if it\u0027s not already captured (assigned an ID) then assign it an ID. If its contents needs to be captured then capture its contents.\n\nPS: this is super pseudo code. Not trying to be correct, just hopefully conveying the idea.\n\n```cpp\nRecordDrawCommand???(...) {\n  for each bindGroup\n    if (bindGroup is not already captured)\n      for each entry in bindGroup\n        CaptureContentsOfResourceIfNeededAndNotAlreadyCaptured(entry.resource)\n      CaptureBindGroup(bindGroup)\n}\n\nRecordBeginRenderPass(...) {\n  RecordableRenderPass rPass;\n  for each [...colorAttachments, depthStencilAttachment]\n    if attachment.loadOp \u003d\u003d \u0027clear\u0027\n      id \u003d RecordTextureIfNotAlreadyRecorded(attachment.view)\n    else\n      id \u003d CaptureTextureIfNotAlreadyCaptured(attachment.view)\n    rPass.addAttachment(id);\n  ...\n  SaveRenderPassInfo(rPass);\n  ...\n}\n\nuint32_t RecordResourceIfNotAlreadyRecorded(Texture texture) {\n  if (!haveIdFor(texture)) {\n    id \u003d getNextId();\n    params \u003d RecordTextureCreationParameters(texture);\n    SaveTextureCreationParametersAndAssociateId(id, params);\n  }\n  return GetIdForTexture(texture);\n}\n\nuint32_t RecordResourceIfNotAlreadyRecorded(TextureView view) {\n   if (!haveIdFor(view)) {\n     viewId \u003d getNextId();\n     textureId \u003d RecordResourceIfNotAlreadyRecorderd(view.texture);\n     params \u003d RecordTextureViewCreationParamters(view);\n     SaveTextureViewCreationParamtersAndAssociateId(id, params);\n   }\n   return GetIdForTextureView(view);\n}\n\nCaptureContentsOfResourceIfNeededAndNotAlreadyCaptured(resource) {\n  // not sure when a resource capture is NOT needed but an example might\n  // be a buffer that was created but has never been written to.\n  // Not sure if that\u0027s tracked. Can leave that for later and just capture\n  // everything\n  if (!hasIdFoResource(resource)) {\n    id \u003d RecordResourceIfNotAlreadyRecorded(resource);\n    if (needCapture(resource)) {\n      capture initial data for resource\n    }\n  }\n  return GetIdFor(resource)\n    \n}\n```\n\nMaybe capturing all objects is a better way to start? Though if we know now that a minimal capture is preferred then switching later would be a big change.",
