      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking out loud, I\u0027d expect to load a recording and then be able to play it up to any point. \n\nIf it makes sense, maybe the thing that plays back the recording should not be the same object as the recording itself?\n\nI don\u0027t have a concrete suggestion. These are just thoughts as I read the code. If it\u0027s one object then I think I\u0027d expect either\n\n```cpp\nReplayer::Load(std::istream \u0026in)\nReplayer::StartPlayback(WGPUDevice device);\n```\n\nIf it\u0027s 2 objects, then I\u0027d expect something like\n\n```cpp\nclass Recording {\n  static Recording* Load(std::istream \u0026in);\n}\n\nclass Replayer {\n  void StartPlayback(WGPDevice device, Recording\u0026 recording);\n}\n```\n\nFollowing what I think I remember of the JS debugger. Maybe something more like\n\n```cpp\nclass Recording {\n  static Recording* Load(std::istream \u0026in);\n}\n\nclass Replayer {\n  static Replayer* Create(WGPDevice device, Recording\u0026 recording);\n  void PlayToPosition(CmdIndex cmdIndex);\n\n  CmdIndex mCurrentIndex;\n}\n```\n\nWhere `PlayToPosition` does something like\n\n```cpp\nvoid Replayer::PlayToPosition(CmdIndex cmdIndex) {\n  if (cmdIndex \u003d\u003d CmdIndex::Start || cmdIndex \u003c mCurrentIndex) {\n    // we need to start the playback so\n    // 1. delete or reset all existing resources (Buffers, Textures)\n    // 2. set all existing resources to the state just before the capture\n    // 3. start playback from beginning\n    mCurrentIndex \u003d CmdIndex::Start;\n  }\n  while (mCurrentIndex \u003c cmdIndex) {\n    Cmd cmd \u003d mPlayback.getCmd(mCurrentIndex++);\n    cmd.Execute(); // \n  }\n}\n```\n\nI don\u0027t know if `Recording` is good vs `Capture` or if it matters.",
      "revId": "eebf9d06d37182048323ad282e4b9205ee0a3493",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
